<title>FRANCE: ONIC cuts 1996/97 soft wheat export goal.</title>
<headline>ONIC cuts 1996/97 soft wheat export goal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's grain office ONIC on Wednesday confirmed it had cut its target for soft wheat exports in the 1996/97 (July/June) season.</p>
<p>In a monthly supply/demand report, it projected France would export 6.25 million tonnes of soft wheat to non-EU countries in 1996/97 compared with a previous estimate of 6.30 million tonnes.</p>
<p>It also cut soft wheat exports to France's partners in the European Union to 9.37 million tonnes from a previous forecast of 9.42 million.</p>
<p>Last year France exported 3.75 million tonnes of soft wheat outside the European Union and 8.613 million tonnes to other European Union countries.</p>
</text>
